experiment: slotmat
  the question      §59a. NOT A TEST. §58 named a re-score on its expression
                    ramp, and §58's own log says that is UNDERPOWERED: one
                    eighth reads SE 0.0338 and FOUR read 0.0297, so width
                    buys 12% and a 2-eighth window is ~0.031 against an
                    averaging prediction of +0.1228 -- 3.96 SE, under the
                    classifier's own A >= 4E gate. This run SIZES that test.
  and the second    §58 found T1.ORACLE -- PINNED, so its index CANNOT
                    collapse -- scoring n 1 of 12 in e8. One byte per probe
                    splits SILENCE from a DARK INDEX, which §56 and §58 both
                    read through a single conflated number.
  THERE IS NO PRIMARY HERE. Nothing below can move §53's null or §58's.
  the window        §59b will use e6-e7, fixed from §58's RAMP in the
                    pre-registration and NOT from the table below. Fallback
                    e5-e7. Affordability limit 96 creatures, stated first.
  session           900.0 s of simulated life x 120 sessions, 4 arms
  instrument        slotmat   trial seed 0000000001357e69   120 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  creatures live  120/120

  THE e8 READING'S FOUR BRANCHES, exercised on synthetic input first. The
  450k smoke found `badf` identically 0 over all 960 creature-eighths, so
  its branch CANNOT be reached by a real row and the first row ever to take
  it would be one carrying the answer.
    dropped 0 nov 0 badf 0 -> PROBES MERELY FEWER        ok  (nothing dropped)
    dropped 8 nov 8 badf 0 -> SILENCE                    ok  (all drops silent -- the shape of the real column)
    dropped 8 nov 0 badf 8 -> UNSCORABLE FRAMES          ok  (all drops unscorable -- UNREACHABLE from real data)
    dropped 8 nov 4 badf 4 -> NEITHER REASON DOMINATES   ok  (an even split picks neither)
    dropped 8 nov 3 badf 2 -> NEITHER REASON DOMINATES   ok  (nov leads but carries under half the drops)
    branches reachable  5/5  PASS

  G0 -- ADDITIVITY, READ FIRST. The per-eighth cells summed over the eight
  eighths must equal the cells accumulated in ONE pass over every probe, and
  both must equal the live `cell_g`/`cell_n`. A window's SLOT TERM is not
  the sum of its eighths' slot terms -- `Gbar_s` is re-estimated over the
  window -- but it IS an exact function of the summed CELLS, and that is the
  identity being tested. It is what licenses re-estimating any window
  offline from the matrix. Pure arithmetic, never budget-gated.
    eighths summed  vs  one pass        2.13e-14   over 3840 cells   PASS
    eighths summed  vs  live cell_g/n   2.13e-14   over 3840 cells   PASS

  G1 -- BOOKKEEPING ON THE LEDGER. Every probe is kept or dropped for at
  least one named reason, and the reasons OVERLAP: a probe can be dark and
  silent at once, so they are counted independently and the overlap is
  printed rather than assumed away. Also checked: `probe_why == 0` is
  exactly `probe_g_ok == 1` on every probe, so the new byte cannot disagree
  with §58's bit about whether a probe scored, and no kept probe lands
  outside slots 0-1, which is what makes the matrix dump lossless.
    kept + dropped == probes           0 bad of 960 creature-eighths   PASS
    why == 0  iff  probe_g_ok == 1      0 mismatched probes   PASS
    kept probes outside slots 0-1       0   PASS

  G2 -- IDENTIFICATION, AND IT IS A REAL GATE. A probe calls
  `observe(object, 0, speak=false, show=TRUE, ...)`, and the pin block is
  gated on `show`, so on a pinned arm the probe sets
  `pin_context_oracle(object)`: `context_present()` is true and
  `active_context()` is the true object for every scored tick. **`ctx_slot`
  therefore CANNOT be -1 on a pinned arm.** Required: dark == 0 in all eight
  eighths on BOTH pinned arms. A non-zero count means the split is labelling
  the wrong quantity and the ledger is void -- which is the whole reason the
  e8 answer below is worth anything.
    T1.ORACLE.D  dark     0     0     0     0     0     0     0     0 
    T1.ORACLE    dark     0     0     0     0     0     0     0     0 
    dark probes on the pinned arms, total   0   over 48 creatures   PASS

