  §58's ITEM 2, ANSWERED. T1.ORACLE is PINNED, so its index cannot
  collapse, and G2 above proves dark == 0 on it. Its e8 column therefore
  says what the late failure IS. The three readings were registered before
  the run: `nov` dominant means SILENCE and points away from the index
  entirely; `badf` dominant means the ruler cannot score real frames; and
  neither dominant means the probes are merely fewer.
    T1.ORACLE e8   probes 216  kept 34  dropped 182   nov 182  badf 0  dark 0
    creatures with >= 6 kept in e8   1 of 12
    READING: SILENCE
    100.0% of e8's drops are probes with no voiced frame at all. The
    late failure on a PINNED index is lost OUTPUT, so it is not about
    the index -- it points at `delivery-fraction`,
    `silence-is-the-homeostat` and §57's surviving homeostasis lead.
    over the WHOLE run: nov 3413, badf 0.  badf is EMPTY, so the split is effectively TWO-WAY
    (dark vs silent) and `formant_error` never refused a frame it was
    given. Its branch was exercised synthetically above, not here.

